# Catalog Core Standards

- Build pages for fast scanning: clear headings, short paragraphs, visible CTAs.
- Keep layouts consistent across sections: same container width, spacing scale, and card rhythm.
- Use component-first structure: extract repeated blocks instead of copying markup.
- Never use emoji as interface icons; use one SVG icon set consistently.
- All interactive elements must have visible hover and focus states.
- Maintain light and dark mode readability with strong text and border contrast.
- Prefer accessible semantics first (`button`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, form labels).
- Keep motion subtle (150-300ms) and respect reduced-motion preferences.

## Delivery Checklist

- Responsive at 375, 768, 1024, and 1440 widths.
- No horizontal scroll on mobile.
- Primary action is obvious in first screen.
- Empty/loading/error states are designed, not left implicit.
